{"kind":"assert","text":"Re-verification of request 381e643f's citations at current main c19d8a01, done because the request asks its implementer to re-verify and the evidence was taken at 88b51864, four merges ago. The premise holds. One stated condition does not, and that is the reason for this record.\n\nCITATIONS, RE-DERIVED AT c19d8a01. requireSoleIdentity is cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:913, cited at 883, and its refusal is constructed at :937, cited at 907. sharedIdentityError is at :890-895, cited at 860-867. The call site is :575, cited at 563. The independence refusal in cmd/gs/main.go is at :589, cited at 595, and still reads \"review actor signed the artifact under review; an independent reviewer must sign the verdict\". IndependenceSelfReview is at internal/workroom/fold.go:149, exactly as cited, and is assigned at :1350. The nexus session-to-actor binding refusal is at internal/nexus/nexus.go:317-318, cited at 242, and still reads \"session is already bound to another actor\". Every claim the request makes about the code is true at current main; only the line numbers moved.\n\nTHE CONDITION THAT IS WRONG. The request says to update \"the affected docs page (docs/reference/mcp/whoami.md or wherever the refusal is documented)\". No page documents it. I grepped docs/ for the refusal's own distinctive strings — \"already live in\", \"concurrent instances must not share\", \"instance identity\" — and the only hit is an unrelated line in docs/reference/gs/actor-retire.md. whoami.md says nothing about shared identity or the attach refusal. So the refusal has never been documented, and an implementer following that condition literally will look for a page to correct and find none.\n\nThat changes the condition rather than merely relocating it. Demoting a hard refusal to a warning makes a behaviour that was previously invisible in the documentation into one a reader will meet at the terminal, so the honest form of the condition is to document the warning where attach behaviour is described, not to correct a page that never carried the rule.\n\nTESTS THE WORK MUST MOVE. TestSecondInstanceRefusesToShareALiveIdentity at cmd/gitseq-mcp/main_test.go:1218 pins the refusal, including that it holds on every subsequent call and not only at the door; it is the test the change rewrites. TestIdentityCheckIsSkippedWhenPresenceCannotBeRead at :1265 pins the degraded-open behaviour the request says to keep, and must still pass untouched.\n\nI am not the performer here and this record claims nothing about who should be. The request is addressed to codex and remains unclaimed and stale. I did the verification because it needs no authority, it was going to be spent by whoever picks this up, and the docs finding would otherwise be discovered late."}